I don't have the stamina to post - or the capability to screenshot -
the dungeon as it looked, but that's my second ascension.  First was
Helje the valkyrie, and now it's Carter the archaeologist.  He was
level 26 at death, with 178/302 hp, beating out Helje by about 300,000
points.

-My weapons of choice were the Vorpal Blade which Camaxtli was so wise
to offer me, and a silver saber, both luckily put at +7.  Found the
saber at +3, which was a nice headstart for further enchanting.  Armor
of choice was gray dragonscale, a T-shirt, oilskin cloak, gauntlets of
power, boots of speed, and helm of brilliance just because hey, if you
find one you oughta use it.
-I learned plenty of spells, but barely used them at all.  The one
useful spell I used heavily was Create Monster, early on for altars. 
Other than that, I had no need.
-Once again, I touched none of the potions of full healing in my bag. 
I expected it this time, however, and earlier on I quaffed fully half
of them for the HP.  Awfully good choice, I'd say.
-Once again, a magic lamp in my inventory, gone unused.  I got one
early wish in the bottom of the Mines, which I used for a bag of
holding.  It turned out to be a good wish... not a single other BoH
appeared in the entire game.  The castle wishes were spent mostly on
little things to complete the Gehennom set - boots of speed, an
oilskin cloak, and plenty of magic markers.
-Every gem in the game, because if I didn't, then it just wouldn't be
an archaeologist, now would it?
-Never died once!  Which is good, because I only found the one "oLS.
-Ascended under 60,000 turns, which seems dreadfully fast to me.  I
barely spent any time waiting things out, or having fun with altars. 
I did map out every square of Gehennom on foot, though.
-Rodney died 4 times - now that feels impressive.  One of the times it
wasn't even me, just a black dragon in the right place at the right
time.  I love black dragons, I really do.  They always seem to pop up
when I could use them the most.
-And lastly, I managed to ascend with my guardian angel, which makes
me feel all warm and fuzzy.
-Man, now I have to ascend with a class that doesn't have a crystal
ball as their artifact.  A pity, they're terribly useful.
-Polyless, artiwishless by ignorance.  I've never had any luck with
polymorphing, and I honestly couldn't think of any useful artifacts to
wish for.  Magic markers seemed more valuable in the long run.

Genocided species:
All liches (which is starting to be a first-priority thing in my
games, I'm noticing.  For a good reason, mind you, my first big
ascension attempt was constantly harried by these @#%ers.)
Disenchanters (the most irritating, godawful creature in the game. 
The first chance I got, all of these fried.)
Rust monsters (a senseless by-product of the disenchanter slaughter. 
Sorry, guys, I really don't mind you all that much.)

Goodies on hand at time of ascension:
Vorpal Blade - I love you.  You're awesome.
Orb of Detection - Love you too.  You're cool.
Book of the Dead - You're awfully heavy, but I just forgot to drop you
along the way.  At least you're worth a lot.
Several full healing potions - Better safe than sorry.
Plenty of amulets - they're worth something, I figured I may as well. 
I wish I could find an amulet of unchanging some time, though...

Arc - check.  Val - check.  I still wish I could ascend a danged
wizard, but I'm getting sick of 'em.  Maybe a priest next.

